course: dictionary
lesson: 8448
title: Sage: a herb, a wise person, or a colour
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: One word can have more than one meaning, and context tells you which one is meant. Look at the words around it. «Sage and onion stuffing is served with roast chicken.» Here sage is a herb, a plant with soft grey-green leaves that cooks use in food.
explain: «The village elder gave sage advice, and everyone listened.» Here sage is an adjective meaning wise, as in «sage advice». A sage can also be a very wise person, often old and respected, like «the wise old sage» who teaches the village.
explain: «Sensible in French means sensitive, but sensible in English is raisonnable or sage.» Here sage means wise and sensible. To check, swap your meaning into the sentence: «wise» still makes sense, so you know you have it right.
fact: Sage (herb) is a plant with soft grey-green leaves, used in cooking.
fact: A sage (noun) can be a very wise person, often an old and respected teacher.
fact: Sage (adjective, formal) means wise, as in «sage advice».
fact: Sage green is a soft grey-green colour.
fact: Sage and onion stuffing is eaten with roast chicken or turkey in the UK and the US.
exercise: «Mum put sage and onion stuffing on the table with the roast turkey.» What is sage in this sentence? | A soft grey-green paint for walls | *A herb used in cooking | A very wise old teacher | A kind of bread
exercise: «The village elder gave sage advice to the lost children.» What does sage mean here? | *Wise | Very old | Loud | Hungry
exercise: The walls were painted sage green. Which colour is sage green? | Pale yellow | *Soft grey-green | Light blue | Bright red
test: «Everyone went to the wise old sage for help.» What does sage mean here? | *A very wise person | Dinner | Herb | Grey-green colour
test: «We planted sage in the garden so we could cook with it.» Which meaning is used? | Sage green | A wise person | *A herb | Sage advice
exam: The walls were painted sage green, and Mia loved the calm colour. In this sentence, what does sage mean? | A herb for cooking | A very wise person | Sensible and wise | *A soft grey-green colour
